    "created_at": "2017-05-18T09:41:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-18T09:41:53Z",
    "body": "To give more context about that interaction with Screen Orientation API: we implemented a feature in the Blink native controls to lock the orientation when the video goes fullscreen using the web events. @foolip told me that with the new event timing, that feature wouldn't work and we needed to have internal callbacks to keep the feature working. The way it was implemented in Blink is exactly the way a website would implement this feature which makes me think it might break some experiences. For example, there was a Web Fundamentals article advertising deeper interactions between fullscreen and orientation changes: https://developers.google.com/web/fundamentals/media/mobile-web-video-playback ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
